# Slice 4 WP3 Deliverable: The ArrivalSink

## 1. Summary of Changes

### A. Refusals Hierarchy (`libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py`)
Extended the `MigrationRefused` hierarchy with the 6 sink-specific typed refusal classes conforming to content-vs-storage discipline:
1. [`JournalPreflightRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L167-L177): Refusal when journal state root or `heads/` directory is unwritable or inaccessible during preflight.
2. [`TargetMismatchOnResumeRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L179-L196): Refusal when resume target diverges from deterministic transform prefix (F2: verification never repairs).
3. [`TornTailRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L198-L208): Refusal when resume target file ends mid-record.
4. [`PublishPreconditionRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L210-L220): Refusal when any of the 5 publication preconditions fails.
5. [`SourceChangedRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L222-L241): Subclass of `PublishPreconditionRefused` asserting source quiescence (content SHA-256 unchanged between inventory snapshot and publication).
6. [`LegacyStorageRefused`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/refusals.py#L243-L253): Refusal when SQLite or filesystem storage operations fail at the engine/driver level.

### B. Migration Sidecar Orchestrator (`libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py`)
Implemented the complete sink lifecycle adhering strictly to the contract seam disciplines:
- **Seam Invariant**: Opens stores strictly through [`BackendRegistry.open(descriptor)`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py#L740-L750), mints first touch via [`ledger.mint(...)`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py#L750-L760), appends drafts via [`ledger.replicate(expected=head, records=...)`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py#L205-L220) through the `AttestedLedger` wrapper. Zero direct `ArrivalLog` write imports.
- **Lineage-Named Staging**: Created at `<store-dir>/<lineage>.arrival` where `<lineage>` is the minted lineage id (no rename at cutover).
- **Stateless Derived Resume**: Re-transforms source, opens existing target, verifies genesis matches lineage, diffs records `1..head.ordinal` against deterministic drafts. Any mismatch or torn tail is a typed refusal (`TargetMismatchOnResumeRefused` / `TornTailRefused`), never a silent repair.
- **Verification Gates**: Asserts BOTH `verify(Full(through=head))` on the target AND the source equivalence re-run (`LegacySource.read(source_path)` vs target records).
- **Migration Report**: Writes `<lineage>.migration-report.json` covering source format, inventory metrics, target head, transform exceptions, equivalence diff, and RFC 8785 canonical JSON bytes signed with custodian key.
- **Report Verification**: [`verify_migration_report(report_path, public_key, *, verify=None, target_path=None)`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py#L550-L640) checks canonical JSON digest signature with injected `Verify` callable (complying with Rule 4 & Rule 11) and verifies live target head match.
- **Atomic Publish**: [`edit_vertex_store_clause(vertex_path, target_location, backend="file")`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp3/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py#L245-L355) verifies all AST fields pre-edit vs post-edit, writes via temporary file in the same directory, calls `os.fsync`, and replaces atomically via `os.replace`.

### C. Test Suite (`libs/migrate/tests/test_sidecar.py`)
Added comprehensive test suite covering all 10 core integration scenarios against real files/SQLite databases:
1. `test_full_roundtrip_synthetic_store` (JSONL and SQLite full pipeline)
2. `test_kill_mid_append_restart_byte_identical` (restarted target is byte-identical to uninterrupted run)
3. `test_resume_against_tampered_target_refuses_no_repair` (F2 gate verification)
4. `test_torn_tail_target_refuses_no_repair` (torn tail refusal)
5. `test_second_migration_after_abandoned_attempt` (fresh lineage on retry without resetting witness)
6. `test_source_mutated_during_staging_refuses_publish` (source quiescence precondition)
7. `test_publish_atomicity_and_crash_simulation` (crash leaves `.vertex` descriptor intact)
8. `test_refused_inventory_creates_no_target` (inventory defect halts pipeline before touching target)
9. `test_journal_preflight_failure_refuses` (journal unwritable pre-flight refusal)
10. `test_legacy_storage_operational_error_wrapped` (SQLite/filesystem operational error wrapped)

